## 5. Architecture and ownership

| Component | Ownership and purpose |
|---|---|
| Environment resource group | Administrator-created prerequisite; never created by workload Terraform |
| Remote backend | Administrator-owned storage; project state key `[[ terraform_state_key ]]` |
| Azure ML workspace | Project-owned, system-assigned identity, identity-based storage access |
| Storage and evidence | Project-owned; Shared Key disabled; evidence container retention [[ evidence_retention_days ]] days |
| Key Vault | Project-owned; RBAC authorization |
| Log Analytics and Application Insights | Project-owned Dev observability |
| Local execution | Default Dev prepare, train, evaluate, package, score, and local-evidence path; no Azure workspace or compute required |
| Azure training compute | [[ execution.training.cloud_fallback.mode if execution.training.cloud_fallback.enabled else 'Disabled; no SKU selected' ]][[ ' using explicit ' ~ execution.training.cloud_fallback.instance_type ~ ', maximum one node' if execution.training.cloud_fallback.enabled else '' ]] |
| Azure batch compute | [[ execution.batch.cloud_fallback.mode if execution.batch.cloud_fallback.enabled else 'Disabled; no SKU selected' ]][[ ' using explicit ' ~ execution.batch.cloud_fallback.instance_type ~ ', minimum zero, maximum one node' if execution.batch.cloud_fallback.enabled else '' ]] |
| Compute identity | [[ 'Project-owned user-assigned identity for enabled cluster compute' if compute_identity_required else 'Not created by the default local-first profile' ]] |
| Workflow identity | Administrator-owned Entra OIDC prerequisite |
| Storage data roles | Workload Terraform; exact project-storage scope for workspace and workflow identities[[ ', plus enabled cluster compute identity' if compute_identity_required else '' ]] |

One resource has one IaC owner. Workload Terraform must not change bootstrap state, the resource group, GitHub/Entra prerequisites, or the backend.

Local lifecycle evidence does not prove Azure ML job submission, managed identity, lineage, registration, endpoint deployment, or batch execution. Every enabled Azure compute workflow requires a deliberate cost-aware authorization phrase. The factory never selects a replacement VM SKU.

